    "section": "Laufer urged the Court to dismiss the case as moot and to refrain from resolving the standing question, characterizing mootness as easy and standing as hard. Acheson urged the Court to decide the standing issue despite mootness, emphasizing the live circuit split and concerns about litigants manipulating the Court's jurisdiction. The Court dismissed the case as moot, vacated the First Circuit's judgment, and remanded with instructions to dismiss, without reaching the standing issue.",
